From af48f95976027eb4f040efbd79d6b429b603e427 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: royka1 <397414+royka1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:50:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] software_isp: Contrast detection autofocus

Focus measure in the CPU statistics (absolute second derivative of green
in the centre half of the window) and an Af algorithm for the simple IPA
with AfMode (manual, auto, continuous; continuous by default), AfTrigger,
LensPosition and AfState: a coarse then fine scan of the lens range with
settle frames after each move, and a rescan in continuous mode when the
focus measure at the chosen position changes for several frames. The lens
is moved directly, also when delayed controls are used, and only when its
position changes; no lens control is sent without a lens.

Based on the software ISP focus control and the autofocus experiments of
Vasiliy Doylov and Pavel Machek (millicam_af_6).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
